Apply a Riemannian trust-region method whose accepted steps use retraction pullback models and whose subproblem solver produces sufficient model decrease whenever either \(\|g_k\|\) is large or \(\lambda_{
min}(\mathcal H_k)\) is negative. Under the stated assumptions, either a second-order critical point is reached finitely or
\[\lim_{k\to\infty}\|g_k\|=0,\qquad \liminf_{k\to\infty}\lambda_{
min}(\mathcal H_k)\geq0.\]
Consequently, every accumulation point at which the Riemannian Hessian is continuous satisfies \(\operatorname{grad}f=0\) and \(\operatorname{Hess}f\succeq0\).
